~ start



PC: Urrrghhh. 
PC: My head hurts…how much did I drink last night?

PC: And what’s that noise?
PC: ...wait. 

PC: Why am I on a train???

IA: Hello our lovely patrons!
IA: While we had our delays, I assure you that we’re now five stops away from the end of the line! 
IA: If you wish to depart the train before then, please make your way to the exit located at the back of the train. 
IA: And as always, thank you for riding with us. 

PC: End of line?
PC: Wait, hey, where am I?

IA: It seems as if a new soul has made their way onto the train.
IA: I see you’re unfamiliar with the way things work around here. 

PC: You can hear me?
PC: Nevermind, that doesn’t matter. What is this? How did I get here?

IA: It’s simple! 
IA: You’re dying. 

PC: Huh…?

IA: Don’t worry, your death will be pretty painless. 
IA: Everything else after won’t be. 

PC: HUH???

IA: Welcome to Death's Transit! 
IA: We’re a public subway line that takes dying souls straight to the pits of hell. 
IA: It’s a one way trip, so once you reach the end of the line- there’s no coming back. 

PC: But I don’t want to die!

IA: That’s what they all say. 
IA: If you want my advice, buckle-in and wait for your destination. 
IA: It won’t be long. 

PC: If I want to stay alive, I need to get off this train before it reaches the end of the line…
PC: Now, where’s the exit? 
=> END